From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:48:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] vl: build the memory map once for board and device creation

Creating a q35 machine with a handful of virtio-pci devices changes the
memory map hundreds of times before the guest runs: 438 flat view
rebuilds were traced on one start.  Outside a transaction each change
regenerates the flat view of every address space and updates KVM's
memory slots, and every slot update is a synchronize_srcu_expedited() in
the host kernel.

Wrap board initialization, device creation and the machine-done
notifiers in a single memory transaction, so the map and the memory
slots are built once, when the machine is complete.  The first system
reset, which copies ROM contents into guest memory, runs from the main
loop after the commit.

The cost is for any device that reads guest memory through an address
space while being realized: it sees the map as it was before the
transaction.  None of the devices this machine creates does.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 system/vl.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/system/vl.c b/system/vl.c
index 061cbdf86..3e0e1852c 100644
--- a/system/vl.c
+++ b/system/vl.c
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #include "qemu/uuid.h"
 #include "system/reset.h"
 #include "system/runstate.h"
+#include "system/memory.h"
 #include "system/runstate-action.h"
 #include "system/seccomp.h"
 #include "system/tcg.h"
@@ -2813,14 +2814,27 @@ static bool qemu_machine_creation_done(Error **errp)
 
 void qmp_x_exit_preconfig(Error **errp)
 {
+    bool ok;
+
     if (phase_check(PHASE_MACHINE_INITIALIZED)) {
         error_setg(errp, "The command is permitted only before machine initialization");
         return;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Creating the board and the devices changes the memory map hundreds of
+     * times, and each change outside a transaction rebuilds the flat view of
+     * every address space and updates KVM's memory slots.  Build the map once,
+     * when the machine is complete.  The first reset, which writes the ROMs
+     * into guest memory, runs after the commit; a device that read guest
+     * memory while being realized would see the map from before this point.
+     */
+    memory_region_transaction_begin();
     qemu_init_board();
     qemu_create_cli_devices();
-    if (!qemu_machine_creation_done(errp)) {
+    ok = qemu_machine_creation_done(errp);
+    memory_region_transaction_commit();
+    if (!ok) {
         return;
     }
 
